      "index": 0,
      "text": "306,800 plus 19,175 equals 325,975.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **767** and **425**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   767 \\times 425 = 767 \\times (400 + 25)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 767 by 400:**\n   \n   \\[\n   767 \\times 400 = 767 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 3,068 \\times 100 = 306,800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 767 by 25:**\n   \n   \\[\n   767 \\times 25 = 767 \\times (20 + 5) = (767 \\times 20) + (767 \\times 5)\n   \\]\n   \n   - **Calculate 767 \u00d7 20:**\n     \n     \\[\n     767 \\times 20 = 15,340\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Calculate 767 \u00d7 5:**\n     \n     \\[\n     767 \\times 5 = 3,835\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Add the two results:**\n     \n     \\[\n     15,340 + 3,835 = 19,175\n     \\]\n\n4. **Add the results from steps 2 and 3:**\n   \n   \\[\n   306,800 + 19,175 = 325,975\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{325,\\!975}\n\\]",
