      "text": "237,000.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **250** and **948**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 250 by 948:**\n\n   \\[\n   250 \\times 948\n   \\]\n\n2. **Break down the multiplication for easier calculation:**\n\n   \\[\n   250 \\times 948 = (200 + 50) \\times 948\n   \\]\n\n3. **Apply the distributive property:**\n\n   \\[\n   = 200 \\times 948 + 50 \\times 948\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate each part separately:**\n\n   - **First part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     200 \\times 948 = 189,\\!600\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Second part:**\n     \n     \\[\n     50 \\times 948 = 47,\\!400\n     \\]\n\n5. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   189,\\!600 + 47,\\!400 = 237,\\!000\n   \\]\n\n6. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{237,\\!000}\n   \\]",
