messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 274 and 272?. I think the correct answer is: 84528\n', '<think>.\nFirst, I recognize that multiplying 274 by 272 directly might be time-consuming. To simplify the calculation, I can use the difference of squares formula, which states that (a + b)(a - b) equals a squared minus b squared.\n\nI notice that 274 is 273 plus 1, and 272 is 273 minus 1. This means I can set a as 273 and b as 1. Applying the formula, the product becomes 273 squared minus 1 squared.\n\nNext, I calculate 273 squared. Breaking it down, 273 squared is (200 + 73) squared, which expands to 200 squared plus 2 times 200 times 73 plus 73 squared. This equals 40,000 plus 29,200 plus 5,329, totaling 74,529. Therefore, my final answer is: ']]
